<% content_for :title, "Models and workflows" %>
<%= turbo_stream_from :learning %>
<h1>Models and workflows</h1>
<p class="prose">
  baible runs any model ComfyUI has. One <code>config/comfy.yml</code> doesn't know runs by where its file is, with generic settings; here the
  language model can propose how it should run instead, and write ComfyUI workflows the builder can't make. Everything it proposes is checked
  against this ComfyUI first, then tried, and baible uses it only once a person accepts it. The language model is never asked during a batch.
</p>
<% unless Llm.enabled? %>
  <p class="alert-text">No language model is set (<%= link_to "Settings", settings_path %>, or <code>LLM_URL</code>): it's what proposes them.</p>
<% end %>
<%= render "learnings/frame" %>
